      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/hoplarchus_psittacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>A large South American cichlid well known to specialised hobbyists but only very rarely offered to the public. Grows up to 40 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/hoplarchus_psittacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This species is only very rarely offered to the public. The animals offered were imported from Colombia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/hoplarchus_psittacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Colombia, Orinoco; Brazil, Rio Negro.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/hoplarchus_psittacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Best kept in large tanks with plenty of hiding places, which they need because of their high interspecific aggression.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/hoplarchus_psittacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This species is relatively sensitive to hole-in-the-head disease, so good aquarium hygiene should have the highest priority.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/hoplarchus_psittacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The optimal water is warm (27 to 30 °C), and preferably soft and acidic.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/hoplarchus_psittacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Omnivorous in nature, so it should be offered plenty of vegetable foods as well.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/hoplarchus_psittacus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Breeding has been reported on several occasions and is a real challenge for the experienced and dedicated fish-breeding hobbyist.</p>"
    }
  ],
